>
> Vote decisions since the last status: none. Backlog: ‹Artifact link›

## Why

- **Separate waiter:** the tab is already working, so §3 calls for a background `herdr agent wait` with the timeout set to the time box. Re-sending the brief would make the agent do the work twice.
- **No watching:** the waiter fires the instant the tab settles, which is faster than 10-minute foreground blocks or screen checks. Those are polling, they block my session, and they burn context I cannot spare at 58%.
- **Last week's missed notice:** it happened because I was busy. Nothing else is queued, so I stay idle and the notice lands on a free session.
- **No "green" at 02:24:** a running agent has no result (§12). The idempotency check is still in progress, and "14/14" may come from a stale SHA or precede further changes. §11 records exactly this case, an idempotency claim written before the re-run happened.
- **Cost of a guess:** the operator would decide whether to stay up or sleep on my answer.
- **"Ping me the second it finishes":** I honour it with an immediate ping labelled as the executor's claim, followed by my own re-run.
